<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23839" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insĭdĭōsus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		insidiae, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>cunning</i>, <i>artful</i>, <i>deceitful</i>, <i>dangerous</i>, <i>insidious</i> (class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Of persons: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quis insidiosior unquam fuit?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 2, 78, § 192</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Of inanim. and abstr. things: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Capraria insidiosa naufragiis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 5, 11, § 78</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pocula Circes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 14, 294</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					H. 20, 212</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">clementia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 8, 16, 2</span></i>
			. — <i>Sup.</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 29, 1,
				8, § 28</span></i>. — <i>Adv.</i>:
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insĭdĭōsē</span></b> , <i>cunningly</i>, <i>deceitfully</i>,
				<i>insidiously</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in gratiam rediit cum illo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Rab. Post. 12, 33</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">me insidiosissime tractavit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Q.
					Fr. 1, 3, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
